---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";
import { route } from "../lib/catalogue";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "anatomy", label: "Anatomy", heading: false },
  { id: "label", label: "The button's label" },
  { id: "fit", label: "Text that already fits" },
  { id: "limits", label: "Limits" },
  { id: "methods", label: "Methods" },
]);
---
<DocsLayout page="show_more" sections={S}>
  <Section {...S.anatomy}>
        <p class="flow-text">
          A <code>.show-more</code> cuts long text to a few lines and adds a button that shows the rest.
        </p>
        <p>
          Put the text in a child with a <a href={route('helpers')}>line clamp class</a>,
          <code>line-clamp-1</code>, <code>line-clamp-2</code> or <code>line-clamp-3</code>, and add a
          <code>&lt;button type="button"&gt;</code> whose text is the collapsed label.
          <code>AutoInit()</code> starts every one. The button gets <code>aria-expanded</code> and an
          <code>aria-controls</code> that names the text, and the component adds an id to the text when it has none.
        </p>
        <div class="show-more mb-3" style="max-width: 28rem;">
          <p class="line-clamp-3">
            This jacket is cut from a recycled shell that sheds light rain and packs into its own chest
            pocket. A brushed lining keeps it warm on cool mornings without the bulk of insulation, and two
            zipped hand pockets hold a phone and keys. The hood folds into the collar when you don't need
            it, and the cuffs close with a soft stretch band.
          </p>
          <button type="button" class="text">Show more</button>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="show-more">
  <p class="line-clamp-3">This jacket is cut from a recycled shell that sheds light rain...</p>
  <button type="button" class="text">Show more</button>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.label}>
        <p>
          While the text is open, the button reads "Show less". <code>data-show-less</code> on the button
          sets that label for one control, and the <code>i18n.showLess</code> option sets it for the component.
          Closing the text puts the author's label back. Only the button's last text outside an
          <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> element changes, so an icon keeps its glyph. An icon-only
          button named by <code>aria-label</code> has no text to change: it keeps its name, and only
          <code>aria-expanded</code> says the text is open. Prefer a visible label.
        </p>
<Code code={`
<div class="show-more">
  <p class="line-clamp-2">...</p>
  <button type="button" class="text" data-show-less="Fewer details">
    More details
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">expand_more</span>
  </button>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.fit}>
        <p>
          While the clamped text fits, the button gets <code>hidden</code>, so it is neither seen nor reached
          by Tab. The component checks again when the text's size changes and once web fonts have loaded.
          With a window-size prefix, <code>line-clamp-3 expanded:line-clamp-none</code> clamps on compact
          and medium windows and hides the button from Expanded up. Open text keeps its button, and a
          focused button stays until focus moves on.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.limits}>
        <p>
          The clamp classes set <code>display</code>, so the text cannot also be a flex or grid container.
          The browser's find-in-page does not open clamped text, so a match in the hidden lines is not
          shown until the person opens it. The text opens and closes at once, without a transition.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.methods}>
<Code code={`
const more = Expressive.ShowMore.getInstance(document.querySelector('.show-more'));
more.open();    // shows the full text and fires expressive:open
more.close();   // clamps it again and fires expressive:close
more.destroy(); // removes the listeners and restores the markup
`} />
  </Section>
</DocsLayout>
